CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ later data member, throwing: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ later data member, non-throwing: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ static member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ const member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
At the declaration, a noexcept operator whose operand names a later
member could not be type-checked and was taken to be true, so the
specifier was never re-evaluated: assertions 1, 3 and 4 failed.  Such a
specifier is now kept and evaluated again with the complete class and,
outside class templates, with `this' bound to the member function's
object (cpp11_member_noexcept_specifier_in_class_template is the class
template case).
